			{
				"property": "",
				"friendlyName": "Start Cooking With Settings",
				"channel": "start_cook",
				"type": "String",
				"refresh": false,
				"actions": [
					{
						"command": "action",
						"parameterType": "JSON",
						"siid": 2,
						"aiid": 5
					}
				],
				"readmeComment": "Starts cooking with a JSON list of 9 values: time (minutes), temperature (degrees Celsius), keep warm after cooking (true or false), recipe id, recipe name, food quantity (1 single layer, 2 double layer, 3 half, 4 full), texture (0 none, 1 crispy roast, 3 degrease), scheduled start time (minutes, 0 starts now), cooking weight (grams). The recipe id is `M0` for manual cooking, `M1` to `M12` for the device presets or `C` plus the recipeID of a cloud recipe. The Mi Home app always sends `u0064u0065u006du006f` as recipe name. Example manual cooking 15 minutes at 180 degrees: `[15,180,false,\"M0\",\"u0064u0065u006du006f\",1,0,0,500]`."
			},
